  "problem": "Rounded to two decimal places, what is the acute angle between the vectors $v=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ \\sqrt{8} \\\\ -2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]$ and $w=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 1 \\\\ \\sqrt{2} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]?$",
  "worked_solution": "Using the formula\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta =\\frac{v\\cdot w}{\u2016v\u2016\\,\u2016w\u2016},\n$$\n\nwe have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta  & =\\frac{{v}_{1}{w}_{1}+{v}_{2}{w}_{2}+{v}_{3}{w}_{3}+{v}_{4}{w}_{4}}{\\sqrt{{v}_{1}^{2}+{v}_{2}^{2}+{v}_{3}^{2}+{v}_{4}^{2}}\\sqrt{{w}_{1}^{2}+{w}_{2}^{2}+{w}_{3}^{2}+{w}_{4}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(1)(4)+(\\sqrt{8})(1)+(-2)(\\sqrt{2})+(-3)(1)}{\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+(\\sqrt{8})^{2}+(-2)^{2}+(-3)^{2}}\\sqrt{(4)^{2}+{1}^{2}+(\\sqrt{2})^{2}+{1}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{22}\\sqrt{20}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{110}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{110}}{220}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}\u2061(\\frac{\\sqrt{110}}{220})\u2248{87.27}^{\u2218}.\n$$",
